5043:
**τέκνον**, -ου, τό 
(τίκτω), [in LXX chiefly for בֵּן, also for יֶלֶד, etc. ;] 
that which is begotten, born (cf. Scottish _bairn_), **a child** of either sex: [[41-mark.13.12|Mrk.13:12]], [[42-luke.1.7|Luk.1:7]], [[44-acts.7.5|Act.7:5]]; pl., [[40-matthew.7.11|Mat.7:11]], [[41-mark.7.27|Mrk.7:27]], [[42-luke.1.17|Luk.1:17]], [[49-ephesians.6.1|Eph.6:1]], al.; τέκνα ἐπαγγελίας, [[45-romans.9.8|Rom.9:8;]] τ. τῆς σαρκός, ib.; in a wider sense (as Heb. בָּנִים), of posterity, [[40-matthew.2.18|Mat.2:18]], [[42-luke.3.8|Luk.3:8]], al.; specif., of a male child, [[40-matthew.21.28|Mat.21:28]], [[44-acts.21.21|Act.21:21]], a,l.; in voc. as a form of kindly address from an elder to a junior or from a teacher to a disciple, [[40-matthew.9.2|Mat.9:2 21:28]], [[41-mark.2.5|Mrk.2:5]], [[42-luke.2.48|Luk.2:48]]; τ. μου (= cl. τ. μοι; see Bl., §37, 5), [[48-galatians.4.19|Gal.4:19]] (τεκνία, WH, txt.), [[55-2-timothy.2.1|2Ti.2:1.]] Metaphorical, 
(a) **of disciples **(apart from direct address, see supr.): Phm 10, [[54-1-timothy.1.2|1Ti.1:2]], [[56-titus.1.4|Tit.1:4]], [[64-3-john.4.1|3Jo.4]]; 
(b) with reference to the Fatherhood of God (see: πατήρ, γεννάω), τέκνα τ. θεοῦ (cf. [[23-isaiah.30.1|Isa.30:1]], Wis.16:21): [[45-romans.8.16|Rom.8:16]], [[49-ephesians.5.1|Eph.5:1]], [[50-philippians.2.15|Php.2:15]]; and esp. in Johannine bks. (cf. Westc, _Epp. Jo._, 94, 120), [[43-john.1.12|Jhn.1:12]], [[62-1-john.3.1|1Jn.3:1]] al.; 
(with) **of those who imitate others and are therefore regarded as the spiritual offspring of their exemplars**: [[40-matthew.3.9|Mat.3:9]], [[42-luke.3.8|Luk.3:8]], [[43-john.8.39|Jhn.8:39]], [[45-romans.9.7|Rom.9:7]], [[60-1-peter.3.6|1Pe.3:6]]; τ. διαβόλου, [[62-1-john.3.10|1Jn.3:10;]] 
(d) as in Heb. (LXX, [[29-joel.2.23|Jol.2:23]], [[19-psalms.149.2|Psa.149:2]], 1Ma.1:38), of the inhabitants of a city: [[40-matthew.23.37|Mat.23:37]], [[42-luke.13.34|Luk.13:34 19:44]], [[48-galatians.4.25|Gal.4:25]]; 
(e) with an adjectival genitive, frequently rendering a Heb. expression, adopted from LXX or formed on the analogy of its language, but sometimes with parallels in Gk. writers (see Deiss., _BS_, 161ff.): τέκνα φωτός, [[49-ephesians.5.8|Eph.5:8;]] τ. ὑπακοῆς, [[60-1-peter.1.14|1Pe.1:14;]] κατάρας, [[61-2-peter.2.14|2Pe.2:14;]] ὀργῆς, [[49-ephesians.2.3|Eph.2:3.]] 
_SYN._: see: παῖς. (AS)

5119:
**τότε**, _demonstr. adv._ of time, correlat. of ὅτε, 
**then, at that time**; 
(a) **of concurrent events**: [[40-matthew.2.17|Mat.2:17 3:5]] and freq., [[45-romans.6.21|Rom.6:21;]] before ptcp., [[40-matthew.2.16|Mat.2:16]], [[48-galatians.4.8|Gal.4:8]]; opposite to νῦν, [[48-galatians.4.29|Gal.4:29]], [[58-hebrews.12.26|Heb.12:26]]; ὁ τ. κόσμος, [[61-2-peter.3.6|2Pe.3:6;]] 
(b) of consequent events, **then, thereupon**: [[40-matthew.2.7|Mat.2:7 3:5 4:1]] and freq., [[42-luke.11.26|Luk.11:26;]] τ. οὖν, [[43-john.11.14|Jhn.11:14 19:1, 16 20:8]]; εὐθέως τ., [[44-acts.17.14|Act.17:14;]] ὅτε . . . τ., [[40-matthew.13.26|Mat.13:26 21:1]], [[43-john.12.16|Jhn.12:16]]; ἀπὸ τ., [[40-matthew.4.17|Mat.4:17 16:21 26:16]], [[42-luke.16.16|Luk.16:16]]; 
(with) **of things future**: [[40-matthew.24.28|Mat.24:28, 40 25:1, 31]]ff.; opposite to ἄρτι, [[46-1-corinthians.13.12|1Co.13:12;]] καὶ τ., [[40-matthew.7.23|Mat.7:23]], [[41-mark.13.21|Mrk.13:21]], [[42-luke.21.27|Luk.21:27]], [[46-1-corinthians.4.5|1Co.4:5]], al.; ὅταν . . . τ., [[40-matthew.9.15|Mat.9:15]], [[41-mark.2.20|Mrk.2:20]], [[42-luke.5.35|Luk.5:35]], [[52-1-thessalonians.5.3|1Th.5:3]], al. (more frequently in Mt than in the rest of the NT). 
(AS)

5192:
**ὑακίνθος**, -ου, ό 
[in LXX chiefly for תְּכֵלֶת ;] 
**hyacinth**; 
(a) in cl., a flower, prob. the dark blue iris; 
(b) **in late writers, a precious stone of the same colour, perhaps the sapphire**: [[66-revelation.21.20|Rev.21:20]] (Phil., FlJ, al.).
(AS)

5207:
**υἱός**, -οῦ, ὁ, [in LXX very frequently and nearly always for בֵּן, [[01-genesis.4.17|Gen.4:17]], al.; for בַּר, [[27-daniel.7.13|Dan LXX TH 7:13]], al.; etc. ;], 
**a son**; 
1. **in the ordinary sense**: [[40-matthew.10.37|Mat.10:37]], [[41-mark.9.17|Mrk.9:17]], [[42-luke.1.13|Luk.1:13]], al. mult.; omitted with the art. of origin (WM, §30, 3; Bl., §35, 2), τὸν τοῦ Ἰεσσαί, [[44-acts.13.22|Act.13:22]] (LXX); also with genitive anarth. (cl.), Σώπατρος Πύρρου Βεροιαῖος, [[44-acts.20.4|Act.20:4;]] with adj., προτότοκος, [[42-luke.2.7|Luk.2:7;]] μονογένης, [[42-luke.7.12|Luk.7:12;]] opposite to νόθος, [[58-hebrews.12.8|Heb.12:8;]] in a wider sense, of posterity: ὁ υἱ. Δαυΐδ, of the Messiah (cf. Dalman, _Words_, 316ff.; _DCG_, ii, 653f.), [[40-matthew.22.42|Mat.22:42, 45]] [[41-mark.12.35|Mrk.12:35, 37]] [[42-luke.20.41|Luk.20:41, 44]] al.; υἱοὶ Ἰσραήλ, (cf. υἷες Ἀχαιῶν, Hom., _Il._, i, 162, al.), [[40-matthew.27.9|Mat.27:9]], [[44-acts.9.15|Act.9:15]], al. 
2. Metaphorical; 
(a) **as belonging to, being connected with or having the quality of that which follows **(a usage mainly due to translation from a Semitic original; cf. Deiss., _BS_, 161ff.; Dalman, _Words_, 115f.; _DCG_, ii, 652f.): τ. πονεροῦ (διαβόλου), [[40-matthew.13.38|Mat.13:38]], [[44-acts.13.10|Act.13:10]]; τ. νυμφῶνος (see: νυμφών), [[40-matthew.9.15|Mat.9:15]], [[41-mark.2.19|Mrk.2:19]], al.; τ. φωτός (Lft., _Notes_, 74), [[42-luke.16.8|Luk.16:8]], [[43-john.12.36|Jhn.12:36]], [[52-1-thessalonians.5.5|1Th.5:5]]; τ. εἰρεήμης, [[42-luke.10.6|Luk.10:6;]] γεέννης, [[40-matthew.23.15|Mat.23:15;]] τ. ἀπωλείας, [[43-john.17.12|Jhn.17:12]], [[53-2-thessalonians.2.3|2Th.2:3]]; τ. αἰῶνος τούτου, [[42-luke.16.8|Luk.16:8 20:34]]; τ. ἀπειθειάς, [[49-ephesians.2.2|Eph.2:2 5:6]]; βροντῆς, [[41-mark.3.17|Mrk.3:17;]] τ. ἀναστάσεως, [[42-luke.20.36|Luk.20:36;]] παρακλήσεως, [[44-acts.4.36|Act.4:36;]] τ. προφητῶν κ. τ. διαθήκης, [[44-acts.3.25|Act.3:25;]] 
(b) υἱὸς τ. θεοῦ (cf. Dalman, _Words_, 268ff.; Deiss., _BS_, 166f.; _DB_, iv, 570 ff.; _DCG_, ii, 654ff.), of men, as partakers of the Divine nature and of the life to come: [[40-matthew.5.9|Mat.5:9]], [[42-luke.20.36|Luk.20:36]], [[45-romans.8.14|Rom.8:14 9:26]], al.; υἱοὶ (κ. θυγατέρες) τ. ὑψίστου, [[42-luke.6.35|Luk.6:35]], [[47-2-corinthians.6.18|2Co.6:18]]; in an unique sense of Jesus, [[40-matthew.4.3|Mat.4:3 8:29 28:19]], [[41-mark.3.4|Mrk.3:4]], [[42-luke.4.41|Luk.4:41]], [[43-john.9.35|Jhn.9:35 11:27]], al.; ὁ Χριστὸς ὁ υἱ. τ. θεοῦ ζῶντος (τ. εὐλογητοῦ), [[40-matthew.16.16|Mat.16:16]], [[41-mark.14.61|Mrk.14:61]]; 
(with) (ὁ) υἱὸς τοῦ ἀνθρώπου (in LXX for Heb. בּן אדם, Aram, בּר אנשׁ; cf. Dalman, _Words_, 234ff.; _DB_, iv, 579ff.; _DCG_, ii, 659ff.; Westc., _St. John_, i, 74ff.; other reff. in Swete, _Mk_, 2:10), based on the Aram. of [[27-daniel.7.13|Dan.7:13]], where the phrase, like the corresponding Heb. (as in [[19-psalms.8.5|Psa.8:5]]), means **a man**, one of the species, and indicates the human appearance of the person in question. It is used of the Messiah in Enoch, with 46, §1-4, also in II [[17-esther.13.3|Est.13:3, 12]], al. Our Lord first makes the phrase a title, using the def. art. It seems to combine the ideas of his true humanity and representative character. Exc. in [[44-acts.7.56|Act.7:56]] and (anarth.) [[66-revelation.1.13|Rev.1:13]] [[66-revelation.14.14|14:14]], it is used of Jesus only by himself: [[40-matthew.8.20|Mat.8:20]], [[41-mark.2.10|Mrk.2:10]], [[42-luke.5.24|Luk.5:24]], [[43-john.1.52|Jhn.1:52]], al. 
(AS)

5215:
**ὕμνος**, -ου, ὁ 
[in LXX for תְּהִלָּה, נְגִינָה, שִׁיר, etc. ;] 
**a hymn**; 
(a) in cl. a festal song in praise of gods or heroes; 
(b) **in LXX and NT a song of praise addressed to God**: [[49-ephesians.5.19|Eph.5:19]], [[51-colossians.3.16|Col.3:16]].
_SYN._: ψαλμός, that which is sung to a musical accompaniment; ᾠδή, the generic term for song (cf. Tr., _Syn._, § LXXviii, Lft. on [[51-colossians.3.16|Col.3:16]]) (AS)

5244:
**ὑπερήφανος**, -ον
(ὑπέρ, φαίνομαι, with η pleonast., see Kühner3, I, 189) [in LXX for זֵד, גֵּאֶה, לוּץ, etc. ;] 
**showing oneself above others**; 
(a) in good sense (Plat., al.), pre-eminent, splendid; 
(b) more frequently in had sense, and so always in Scr., **arrogant, haughty, disdainful **(see Westc. _Epp. Jo._, 65b): [[45-romans.1.30|Rom.1:30]], [[55-2-timothy.3.2|2Ti.3:2]]; διανοίᾳ καρδίας, [[42-luke.1.51|Luk.1:51;]] opposite to ταπεινός (as in [[20-proverbs.3.34|Pro.3:34]]), [[59-james.4.6|Jas.4:6]], [[60-1-peter.5.5|1Pe.5:5]]" (LXX) .
_SYN._: ἀλαζών, ὑβριστής, see Tr., _Syn._, § xxix (AS)

5465:
**χαλάω**, -ῶ 
[in LXX: ([[24-jeremiah.38.6|Jer.38:6]]) (שָׁלַח pi.), etc. ;] 
(a) **to slacken, loosen**; 
(b) **to let loose, let go**; 
(with) **to lower, let down**: with accusative of thing(s), [[41-mark.2.4|Mrk.2:4]], [[42-luke.5.4|Luk.5:4-5]], [[44-acts.9.25|Act.9:25 27:17, 30]]; with accusative of person(s) (cf. Je, l.with), pass., [[47-2-corinthians.11.33|2Co.11:33.]]
(AS)

5587:
**ψιθυρισμός**, -οῦ, ὁ
(ψιθυρίζω, to whisper), [in LXX: [[21-ecclesiastes.10.11|Ecc.10:11]] (לַחַשׁ) * ;] 
**a whispering**; 
(a) of secret slander, [[47-2-corinthians.12.20|2Co.12:20]] (Plut.); 
(b) of a murmured enchantment, Ec, l.with
(AS)
